From 555602fe9832ab63a3706d178517661d0ce7c380 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gambot <56745325+GbotHQ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 11:08:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] gui: leave the application-wide stylesheet to the code
 that owns it

MainWindow::onThemeUpdated() set the generated sheet twice - once application-wide and once on
the window. The application-wide call is not a duplicate of the window one: it *replaces* the
sheet that GUIResources::applyAppearance() installs immediately before every onThemeChanged
emission, which is where the app-wide dialogbutton.ssa comes from. That sheet exists precisely
to style parentless dialogs, and it carries the tree's only QPushButton#browser rules, so the
file-picker button in the new-project dialog lost its styling.

Drop the application-wide call and keep the window one. The font it was there for is already
set application-wide by QApplication::setFont, which Qt documents as inherited by existing and
future children; only that call was ever needed for the parentless dialogs.
---
 src/gui/MainWindow.cpp | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gui/MainWindow.cpp b/src/gui/MainWindow.cpp
index 0c74ab5..b326cbd 100644
--- a/src/gui/MainWindow.cpp
+++ b/src/gui/MainWindow.cpp
@@ -534,8 +534,14 @@ void MainWindow::onThemeUpdated(theme::Theme& aTheme) {
             }
 
         }
-        qDebug() << "fontOption: " << fontOption;
-        qApp->setStyleSheet(fontOption + standard);
+        // Only the window is styled here. The application-wide sheet belongs to
+        // GUIResources::applyAppearance(), which installs dialogbutton.ssa so that parentless
+        // dialogs (QMessageBox and friends) inherit it - and that call runs immediately before
+        // every theme change reaches this function. Setting the application sheet from here
+        // therefore *replaced* it, taking the tree s only QPushButton#browser rules with it and
+        // leaving NewProjectDialog s file-picker button unstyled. The font itself is already
+        // applied application-wide by QApplication::setFont a few lines above, which Qt
+        // documents as inherited by existing and future widgets, so nothing is lost.
         this->setStyleSheet(fontOption + standard);
     }
 
